_vrf_PLAT241_DATA_MON_a          
;
PROBLEM: High 'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of O11 Check
RESPONSE: The high Ueq values for O11 and O12 are due to the disorder 
and increased thermal motion of the formate oxygen atoms.
;
_vrf_PLAT242_DATA_MON_a          
;
PROBLEM: Low 'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of Zn1 Check
RESPONSE: The lower Ueq value for Zn1 arises from its intrinsic lower 
thermal motion compared to neighboring lighter atoms. Refinement 
confirms no significant structural issues.
;
_vrf_PLAT430_DATA_MON_a          
;
PROBLEM: Short Inter D...A Contact O12 ..N3 . 2.82 Ang.
RESPONSE: The short O12...N3 contact 2.82 Ang. likely indicates weak 
hydrogen bonding or disorder. The geometry aligns with the refined 
structural model.
;
